Ink is Iron’s ink. Codex does not add its own bottles — it reads `irons_spellbooks:common_ink` through `legendary_ink`.

## Matching rarity

Each next tier wants **one ink** of the rarity that Iron’s assigns to that spell level, plus XP. Common ink will not unlock a legendary rank. The ink row under the Codex is the filter: select a rarity and **+** buttons that need a different rarity go dull.

| Rarity | Ink item |
| --- | --- |
| Common | `irons_spellbooks:common_ink` |
| Uncommon | `irons_spellbooks:uncommon_ink` |
| Rare | `irons_spellbooks:rare_ink` |
| Epic | `irons_spellbooks:epic_ink` |
| Legendary | `irons_spellbooks:legendary_ink` |

## Craft path

<div class="wiki-item">
<img src="/images/spell-codex/blank_codex_page_rare.png" alt="Empty Codex Page" width="40" height="40" />
<div>
<strong>1. Arcane Anvil</strong>
<p>Paper + ink → Empty Codex Page attuned to that ink. Tooltip: “Arcane Anvil: paper + ink -> Empty Codex Page”.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="wiki-item">
<img src="/images/spell-codex/codex_page.png" alt="Codex Page" width="40" height="40" />
<div>
<strong>2. Scroll Forge</strong>
<p>Hold a school focus in one hand and the Empty Codex Page in the other. Right-click the Scroll Forge. Pays <strong>10 levels</strong> of XP, eats the focus and the blank, gives a Codex Page for a random undiscovered spell in that school.</p>
</div>
</div>

If imprint fails:

- “Need 10 levels worth of XP…” — earn more XP first
- “No spells in this school match … ink” — use a higher rarity blank
- “You already know every spell this … Empty Codex can imprint” — raise blank rarity or pick another school
- “That school is blocked on this server” — school is in `school_blacklist.json`

## XP costs (defaults)

Tier I is free on discover. Higher tiers:

- Default formula: `20 + 10 × tier` levels-worth from level 0
- Override per school: `config/specs_irons_spellbooks/school_unlock_costs.json`
- Override per spell: `spell_unlock_costs.json` (wins over school)
- Focus discount: **25%** off XP only

## Recycle

Finished Codex Pages you do not need go in an **Alchemist Cauldron** for ink. Better than letting duplicates sit in a chest.
